1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,690
For five seconds nothing on Earth

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:03,830
can grip anything, and Gus slides

3
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:05,440
twenty feet without taking a step.

4
00:00:05,484 --> 00:00:07,044
It's nine on a Sunday morning

5
00:00:07,274 --> 00:00:08,594
and Gus is shoving a heavy

6
00:00:08,604 --> 00:00:10,254
flowerpot across his garden.

7
00:00:10,298 --> 00:00:11,838
It scrapes and sticks and he

8
00:00:11,848 --> 00:00:13,208
wishes friction would just go

9
00:00:13,218 --> 00:00:13,688
away.

10
00:00:13,732 --> 00:00:15,082
His wife says he'd miss it.

11
00:00:15,352 --> 00:00:16,652
His neighbor says life would be

12
00:00:16,662 --> 00:00:17,332
a breeze.

13
00:00:17,386 --> 00:00:18,996
Then for five seconds Gus gets

14
00:00:19,006 --> 00:00:19,596
his wish.

15
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:20,860
The pot glides off like a

16
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:21,780
puck on ice.

17
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:23,630
But his feet can't push, so

18
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:24,730
he runs on the spot.

19
00:00:24,774 --> 00:00:26,244
His wife's cup slips right through

20
00:00:26,254 --> 00:00:27,714
her fingers and the neighbor's

21
00:00:27,724 --> 00:00:29,564
ladder slides flat down the wall.

22
00:00:29,618 --> 00:00:30,928
Then the whole garden starts to

23
00:00:30,938 --> 00:00:32,618
drift, all the same way.

24
00:00:32,662 --> 00:00:34,032
But the lawn looks flat.

25
00:00:34,042 --> 00:00:35,112
So what's pulling them?

26
00:00:35,156 --> 00:00:36,676
You see, no lawn is flat.

27
00:00:37,016 --> 00:00:38,336
Builders tilt it half an inch

28
00:00:38,346 --> 00:00:39,836
a foot so rain runs away

29
00:00:39,846 --> 00:00:40,626
from the house.

30
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:41,990
That slope tugs at Gus with

31
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,450
nine pounds all day long.

32
00:00:43,494 --> 00:00:45,074
Ever pressed two brushes together?

33
00:00:45,344 --> 00:00:46,364
Up close his feet and the

34
00:00:46,374 --> 00:00:48,104
grass are bristles too, and they

35
00:00:48,114 --> 00:00:48,484
lock.

36
00:00:48,528 --> 00:00:50,158
Take that away and nine pounds

37
00:00:50,168 --> 00:00:50,838
is plenty.

38
00:00:51,158 --> 00:00:52,878
Heavy or light, everything speeds

39
00:00:52,888 --> 00:00:54,648
up alike: twenty feet in five

40
00:00:54,658 --> 00:00:55,288
seconds.

41
00:00:55,342 --> 00:00:56,772
Luckily, friction comes back.

42
00:00:56,826 --> 00:00:58,696
Unluckily it grabs his feet and

43
00:00:58,706 --> 00:01:00,146
the rest of Gus keeps going

44
00:01:00,156 --> 00:01:01,286
at a jogging pace.

45
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:02,140
And his pot?

46
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:03,800
It stops twenty feet too far.

47
00:01:03,854 --> 00:01:05,044
Gus drags it all the way

48
00:01:05,054 --> 00:01:07,114
back and never complains again.
